WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.360
Pietro Wilson tossed and turned as the nightmares
from the previous day filled his dreams.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.060
In his restless sleep he watched the slaughter
of his colleagues at Site-22.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:15.300
The unknown men who entered the facility had
gunned down everyone who worked there, everyone

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.610
except Pietro.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.250
He remembered running deeper into the facility,
only to be cornered in a windowless concrete

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.250
room.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:28.090
There he had found SCP-5000, an exclusionary
suit, that allowed him to become undetectable

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.320
to human senses.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.960
It was a step beyond invisibility.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.420
He successfully made it out of Site-22, but
the eyes of the men he killed to get away

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.600
haunted him.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.170
Pietro had never taken a life before.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:44.089
The only solace was that it felt like the
suit he was wearing had taken over, so his

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:46.840
actions were not technically his own.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.889
But he had to wonder, what would he have done
without the suit?

00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:53.440
Would he still have killed another human to
escape?

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.600
After leaving the facility Pietro had made
his way to an SCP safehouse.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.319
This was where he now lay.

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:04.089
The slaughter of hundreds at Site-22 was bad,
but what he found when he turned on the news

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:06.480
at the safehouse was worse.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.190
SCPs had been let loose around the world and
were killing people by the millions.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.510
What was going on?

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.830
Pietro was startled awake from a nightmare.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:20.680
He was hyperventilating, but his body almost
immediately recovered, and his breathing slowed.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.460
A heads up display flashed on infront of his
eyes.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.890
Pietro Wilson was still contained within SCP-5000.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.420
The suit would not let him go.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.900
He instinctively went to rub his eyes, but
the metal hands of the suit just clanked against

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.790
the helmet that covered his head.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.940
He wanted out of this suit!

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.700
Pietro stood up and walked over to the television.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.159
He reached out to turn it on but paused.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:50.210
He thought: Do I really want to see how bad
things have gotten since I fell asleep?

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.810
But he had to know.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.770
He was filled with dread as the TV came on
and he saw the first images.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:00.740
The world looked as if it was ending, and
it seemed like the SCP Foundation was responsible.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.420
How could this be?

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.020
They were supposed to protect humanity not
destroy it.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.599
Pietro needed to uncover the truth behind
what was happening.

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:16.540
SCP-5000 had a log entry function that he
could use to record everything he uncovered.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.980
Even if he didn’t make it out of this alive,
maybe one day someone would find the suit

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.700
and be able to access what he had learned.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.540
The date of his first journal entry was February
1, 2020.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.269
As Pietro watched the carnage unfold on TV,
he began to put together the pieces of what

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:34.029
he had witnessed himself.

00:02:34.029 --> 00:02:38.799
He knew a special-ops squad had executed everyone
at Site-22 where he worked.

00:02:38.799 --> 00:02:41.180
He knew that the SCPs had been let loose.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.079
He knew the world was ending… but why?

00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:47.779
As Pietro pondered this, a newscaster appeared.

00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:51.950
“What you have just witnessed are reports
from around the world of monsters ravaging

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.769
cities and towns.

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:57.670
This all started with a mysterious message
from an organization that calls itself the

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.420
SCP Foundation.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.989
Their ruling body, named the O5 Council, released
the following statement: ‘For those who

00:03:03.989 --> 00:03:08.849
are not currently aware of our existence,
we represent the organization known as the

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:10.550
SCP Foundation.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.980
Our previous mission centered around the containment
and study of anomalous objects, entities,

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.110
and other assorted phenomena.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:22.099
This mission was the focus of our organization
for more than one-hundred years.

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:27.019
Due to circumstances outside of our control,
this directive has now changed.

00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:31.109
Our new mission will be the extermination
of the human race.

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:33.129
There will be no further communication.”

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:35.830
He couldn’t believe what he was seeing.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.480
The SCP Foundation had declared war on the
human race.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.060
How could this be?

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:45.700
What had led to the O5 council changing their
entire mission from protecting humanity to

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.700
ending it?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.349
Could it be possible that a powerful SCP had
taken control or influenced the council’s

00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:52.349
decision?

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:56.290
Pietro turned on the radio, flipped through
TV channels, and scoured the internet for

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:00.049
information on what had happened over the
past 24 hours.

00:04:00.049 --> 00:04:04.970
The first image he saw was a human-like creature
with arms and legs twice as long as they should

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:10.159
have been, with deep black eyes, and a mouth
curled up into a silent scream showing teeth

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:12.529
as sharp as razor blades.

00:04:12.529 --> 00:04:18.160
From the files he could access Pietro learned
that this was SCP-096, a creature that was

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.660
docile until someone saw its face, at which
point the SCP would start to shriek and cry,

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.600
before hunting down whoever saw its face and
slaughtering them.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.320
He quickly changed the channel.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:34.100
The file said that even if SCP-096 was seen
on a screen, it would find the viewer and

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.990
tear them limb from limb.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.350
Surely that couldn’t be true.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.900
There were potentially millions of people
who had just seen it on TV.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.110
What would happen to them?

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.200
What would happen to him?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.040
On the next channel was footage of a gigantic
animal in the middle of the ocean.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.010
This was SCP-169, a leviathan from the Pre-Cambrian
era.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:58.970
The creature was around 5,000 kilometers long
and slowly swam just below the surface of

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.090
the ocean.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:05.250
The feed suddenly changed to footage of devastating
tsunamis and destruction caused by earthquakes.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:10.230
When SCP-169 had been awoken from its slumber
by the Foundation detonating nukes on its

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.100
back, it began trying to escape the danger.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.120
The movement of the massive creature caused
natural disasters, destroying coastal communities

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.950
around the world.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:24.580
On another channel Pietro watched as the chancellor
of Germany gave a speech, announcing that

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.080
the country was declaring war on the SCP Foundation.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.550
Off camera the sound of a tinkling bell could
be heard.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:35.020
A man dressed as a Victorian era butler entered
and picked up a pen from the Chancellor's

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.870
desk.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.850
He approached the Chancellor and raised the
pen in the air as the camera cut away, but

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:44.480
the sound of gunshots and yelling could be
heard before the feed went dead.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:49.180
The news reported that similar events involving
world leaders by the exact same butler had

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.750
been occurring since the SCP Foundation changed
its mission.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:56.210
Pietro searched through the suit’s files
to try and figure out what was happening and

00:05:56.210 --> 00:06:00.390
found that SCP-662 must have been connected.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:05.710
Next was a strange skin disease plaguing New
York and Delhi designated SCP-610 that covered

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:10.560
its host in rashes and boils before seeking
to take over their bodies.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.400
Finally some good news though, as the outbreak
looked to be contained by the combined efforts

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.840
of the Global Occult Coalition and the Church
of the Broken God.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:23.340
And then some bad news, as SCP-682 had also
been released.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:28.250
A massive crocodilian monster, it’s sole
mission was to destroy all life.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:33.740
It was fueled by hatred for living things,
making it the perfect tool of the O5 Council’s

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.150
new stated mission.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:40.470
Pietro had heard rumors of SCPs that could
instantly end the world, but clearly the Foundation

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:43.700
hadn’t gone down this route… yet.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.620
Did they want to keep the rest of the planet
intact, or maybe there were hold outs in the

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:53.120
SCP Foundation who were trying to stop the
O5 Council from carrying out their mission?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:58.950
All Pietro knew was that right now, there
were some real nasty SCPs running around wreaking

00:06:58.950 --> 00:06:59.950
havoc.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.490
Pietro suddenly heard an explosion in the
distance.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.910
Far away, but still close enough to make him
nervous.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:09.650
Maybe he was better off staying in the safehouse
and waiting out the apocalypse.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:14.030
The suit was keeping him healthy, nourished,
and undetectable to foes.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.990
Any sane person would have remained there
in seclusion and safety, but Pietro needed

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.170
answers.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:24.090
He felt it was his responsibility to log and
try to make sense of everything the SCP Foundation

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.090
was doing.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.590
He brought up a map of SCP sites in the area
on his display.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.770
The closest was Site-19.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:34.930
It was time to venture out into the end of
the world and find some answers.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:39.100
But he was about to be faced with even more
questions.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:43.590
On the way to Site-19, Pietro came across
something strange - a squad of Foundation

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.100
soldiers in a clearing.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:50.020
They were standing at attention as their commander
paced back and forth, up and down the line.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:54.750
The soldiers' uniforms had the insignia “MTF
Epsilon-6” embroidered on them.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:58.410
The commander stopped in front of the first
soldier in the line, clapped her hands, and

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.590
informed the soldier she would be beginning
the check now.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:05.620
The commander pulled out a long knife and
plunged it into the soldier’s shoulder.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:11.150
Strangely, the soldier did not move, make
a sound, or react in any way.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:14.270
She moved to the next soldier and repeated
the same process.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:17.570
This continued down the line until she reached
the eighth soldier.

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:22.610
This time when the commander stabbed the shoulder
of the soldier, he noticeably winced and cried

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:23.770
out in pain.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.139
The commander shouted “got a live one!”

00:08:26.139 --> 00:08:30.210
Pietro watched as the soldiers raised their
guns and fired at the one who had cried out.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.180
He dropped to the ground.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:35.479
The commander moved on to the last soldier
and put the knife in his shoulder.

00:08:35.479 --> 00:08:37.140
There was no reaction.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:39.330
“Alright we’re clear,” yelled the commander.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.310
“Let’s move out!”

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:45.920
Pietro waited until the squad was out of sight
and made his way to the corpse lying on the

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:46.920
ground.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.920
He scavenged weapons and basic medical supplies,
then he buried the body and recorded what

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.400
he had seen in SCP-5000’s log.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:58.670
He had no idea why this soldier was killed,
or why the others didn’t feel pain.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.570
Maybe they weren’t human at all?

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.080
Maybe it was a squad of SCPs that had a human
infiltrate their ranks?

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.440
None of this makes sense, Piertro thought,
before continuing on.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:15.040
Upon reaching Site-19, Pietro found it in
disarray, and worse, practically all of the

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.370
SCPs that were held at the site had breached
containment.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:23.800
He was able to walk into the compound unnoticed
and deep in the facility he found scientists

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:27.770
and researchers going about their business
as if they had no idea what was happening

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.261
out in the world.

00:09:29.261 --> 00:09:32.110
They must have been following the orders of
the O5 Council.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:36.180
Pietro listened in on conversations about
how to create the maximum number of human

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:39.900
casualties, and which SCP should be released
next.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:43.150
He felt a deep hatred for the people in this
facility.

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:47.550
How could they be so casual about wiping out
humanity?

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:51.680
As he observed more of the workers at Site-19,
he noticed something strange.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:56.700
Everyones’ eyes were cold and dead, like
there was no humanity left in them, as if

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.190
something had gotten to these scientists and
removed the very souls from their bodies.

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:05.440
Pietro stealthily stole a senior staff member’s
credentials and found an empty office where

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:09.710
he could access logs from the facility, to
try and get a better idea of the timeline

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:14.310
of events that led to the SCP Foundation’s
war on humanity.

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:18.440
He logged into the mainframe and brought up
entries from the end of the previous year.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:23.110
He found that late in 2019 a project called
‘PNEUMA’ became of great interest to the

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.540
O5 council.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:28.130
From what Pietro could tell, the project had
something to do with the collective human

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.279
consciousness, also called the psychospace.

00:10:31.279 --> 00:10:36.270
Apparently, SCP researchers had a breakthrough
in mapping out the psychospace.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:40.360
Unfortunately, many of the files had been
redacted, and there was no way for Pietro

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.270
to access the unredacted version.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:46.710
After ‘PNEUMA’ had been brought to the
attention of the O5 Council, a series of orders

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:52.050
were sent to all senior staff and site directors
but frustratingly these orders had also been

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.050
redacted.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:57.339
All he could see was that after the orders
were sent out, a wave of resignations were

00:10:57.339 --> 00:10:59.440
submitted across the Foundation.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:04.980
Suspiciously, a wave of suicides had also
occurred at roughly the same time.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.560
What was in these orders?!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.900
The 05 council then sent out a number of files
to all senior staff and site directors with

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:15.630
instructions to disseminate the materials
among those serving under them, after which

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:19.210
both the resignations and deaths immediately
ceased.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:24.800
Pietro searched everywhere for what was in
those files, but like so much of the SCP database,

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.529
this information had been redacted as well.

00:11:27.529 --> 00:11:31.910
What was clear was that the SCP Foundation
had begun gearing up for the extermination

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:34.440
of humanity the following year.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:40.410
The entry log for February 1, 2020 read: “Mobile
Task Forces are dispatched to all Exclusionary

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:43.280
Sites to execute all personnel.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:47.730
Immediately following the conclusion of these
missions, the Foundation declares war on humanity.”

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:51.339
This was where Pietro Wilson’s journey had
started.

00:11:51.339 --> 00:11:54.620
He slammed his hands down on the computer
monitor in frustration.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:58.899
The suit absorbed all of the impact and crushed
the monitor in half.

00:11:58.899 --> 00:12:02.710
Pietro moved to a new, non smashed computer,
and logged in again.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:07.380
This time he brought up the most current entries
to see what the O5 Council was up to recently

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.750
to see if there were some answers in the present.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.500
The SCP Foundation had been busy while he
was making his way to Site-19.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:19.680
They had released SCP-1048 in Paris, which
now led a horde of bears down the Champs Elysées.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.750
In the distance Pietro thought he could almost
make out a massive red teddy bear walking

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.540
between the buildings.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:30.860
The SCP Foundation was also launching counterattacks
on any organization that tried to oppose them.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:35.670
They used SCP-1290 to hurl projectiles at
the Global Occult Coalition’s base.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:40.029
They were also using SCP-1440 to brainwash
people and convince them that they needed

00:12:40.029 --> 00:12:41.029
to riot.

00:12:41.029 --> 00:12:45.390
This caused widespread destruction as people
panicked and were trampled to death.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:50.220
Pietro thought it was sad that such a kind
looking old man could cause so much destruction.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:54.900
He recorded as much as he could before deciding
that it was time to get out of Site-19.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:13:00.210
Although SCP-5000 still made him undetectable,
he couldn’t shake the feeling that the lifeless

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:05.340
eyes of the staff were beginning to look his
way more and more often.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:11.440
As Pietro exited Site-19, the sky glowed orange
with the fire of countless burning buildings.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.410
He needed to find more answers.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:18.220
He needed to uncover the reason the SCP Foundation
was trying to wipe out humanity.

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:22.500
He had learned a lot from Site-19, and was
sure that if he could just get to the next

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:26.760
site, he would finally be able to figure out
the Foundation’s motive, and maybe even

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.200
how to stop them.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.570
He took a step forward but his heads up display
suddenly went completely dark.

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:37.010
The suit constricted tighter around his body,
slowing the blood flow to his brian.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:44.140
He couldn’t move as his vision got dimmer,
and dimmer, and dimmer, until he blacked out.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.940
Pietro woke to find himself halfway across
the country.

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:51.279
It had been three months since he had been
at Site-19, and he had no recollection of

00:13:51.279 --> 00:13:53.640
anything that had happened since.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.850
His body had taken a toll in those months.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:01.790
He had new scars and a bandage wrapped around
his head, but the SCP-5000 suit did not seem

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:03.810
to have a scratch on it.

00:14:03.810 --> 00:14:08.690
Strangest of all though, was the briefcase
that Pietro had in his hand, and the uncontrollable

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:12.760
need to deliver it to the mysterious SCP-579.

